WEBVTT

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.820
Mama...

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.690
He caused Freecell such sadness.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.710
He has broken Freecell.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.010
You want to play a game
with Kaito Daimon?

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.820
Huh, well, well...

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.620
To have a man like you,
with such motivation,

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.430
gives me pride as your director.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.350
However!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.420
Remember this well.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.470
You are a whelp, unfit to
speak your opinions to me!

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:08.810
How did it go, Mr. Pinochle?

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.790
Lost

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.920
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.840
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.760
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.100
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.810
Found

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.060
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.520
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:58.360
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.450
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.780
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.700
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.410
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.750
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.960
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.330
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.800
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.510
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.340
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:25.220
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.350
It's now or never

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:28.430
That is what they say

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:30.520
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.190
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.350
That is what they say

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.520
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.030
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.240
That is what they say

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.660
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.000
Pinochle's Resolve

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.030
So, you're tellin' me  the truth?

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.380
Yes, if you win this game,

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.280
I'll tell you everything.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.620
About what happened
with you and Freecell.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.510
A Replica?!

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.470
Yes, without a doubt,
Eve's Ring was a Replica.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.040
Impossible!

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.560
A chosen one of the Orpheus Order
wouldn't get a Replica Ring!

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.750
But I'm certain it was.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.130
Jeez, Sis!

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:42.280
What's the big idea, leaving
me out of the loop?

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.180
This has nothing to do with you.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.330
Go away.

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:59.710
The Orpheus Order may
have something we're unaware of.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.250
If so, that, too, is
by Mr. Klondike's will.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.770
Please wait a little
longer, Mr. Freecell.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.030
I know, Whist.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:21.990
I'm the only one who can
begin puzzle time with Kaito.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.740
The true puzzle time, that is.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.540
I'm relieved to hear that.

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:31.390
What do you say?

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.220
Shall we do this together?

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.540
Let's have a look at
something interesting.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.560
What do you think?

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.120
This is the game that I've made.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.560
I call it, "Inferno Tower."

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.930
There are thirteen levels up this tower.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.420
Each level has a color-matching puzzle.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.320
To clear the puzzle,
match all the colors of all areas on the dials.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.560
When on the same level at once,

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:15.710
you and I will be given the same problem.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.560
Of course, whoever solves it first wins.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.420
The loser goes up to the
next level via a lift.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:25.820
With each successive level,
the problems' difficulty increases.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:31.180
In the end, whoever reaches
the top level first wins.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.870
So, Pinochle this time, huh?

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:42.780
Yes, it's the will of
Mr. Klondike himself.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.340
He said that?

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:47.930
I thought Pinochle couldn't
do anything on his own.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.880
According to our latest data,

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.830
Mr. Pinochle's Ring has been upgraded
to an Orpheus Ring Gamma.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.890
So, he will be completely
absorbed by the Ring, eh?

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.690
Too bad...

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.840
for the Replica.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.090
Now then, shall we begin?

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:07.990
Yeah.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.580
Inferno Tower...

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:10.590
Play!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.170
Be careful, Kaito!

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.030
He might try babblin' a
bunch of weird crap again,

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:55.310
tryin' to get you off guard!

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.660
Don't you worry about that.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.080
I will say no lies or trickery.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.550
Today, I am in earnest.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:08.820
What is that?

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.700
A blast furnace?!

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.060
When the winner reaches
the top and wins again,

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:21.750
the loser's lift will
be turned upside-down.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:23.580
Bastard!

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.090
I told you, didn't I?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.730
I will defeat you for real,

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:33.430
erase you from this world...

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.510
Kaito Daimon!

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:37.830
You can't!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.180
This puzzle is too dangerous!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.330
That's right!

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.940
Even if Kaito wins, the
other guy will be...

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.900
It can't be stopped!

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.600
Just what are you after?

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.290
Why would you do this?!

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:04.440
Kaito Daimon has hurt others,
walked all over them...

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.380
It's only right he be erased.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.230
You're talking about
that Freecell person?

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:13.240
Kaito broke his promise with Freecell,

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.350
and Freecell's mother died.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.200
Kaito's hand paused!

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.270
That idiot!

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:25.370
Freecell cared for his mother.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:27.540
He loved her!

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.480
And yet...

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:32.090
It may be true that
Kaito broke his promise,

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:34.470
and that Freecell's mom died,

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.110
but still!

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.300
That's right!

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:39.700
Just how are those two things connected?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.320
I will tell you that
if Kaito Daimon wins.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.670
Just before I die, yes?

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.940
When you know the truth,

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:53.880
you will bear the weight of your sin!

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.890
The sin of having killed me!

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.160
Kaito!

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.970
Stick it to him, Kaito!

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:05.150
What's more, Kaito Daimon is a liar.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.230
A liar?

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:11.650
That's right, Kaito Daimon is a liar.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.820
His lies wounded Freecell!

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:18.800
After breaking his promise,

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.620
he spread vicious rumors about Freecell
to make himself look good.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:25.730
He got in good with everyone else
so that they'd believe his lies.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:29.040
Such lies, such impudence!

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.000
Kaito wouldn't do something like that!

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:35.360
That bastard, talkin' crap again!

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.010
No...

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.240
It's a lie, but it's not a lie.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:43.520
It's a lie, but it's the truth.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.390
A lie, but the truth?

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.020
That's just how you are, Kaito Daimon.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:53.590
You break promises, tell
lies, betray others,

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.780
have wounded so many people!

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:04.290
Now, here, you'll pay for your sins!

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:07.920
Kaito!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.830
Begone!

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.300
Begone already, Kaito Daimon!

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.050
You may be right.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.680
When I was at Crossfield Academy,

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.770
I may have been a terrible person.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.850
I didn't open my heart up to anyone.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:27.480
But that...

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:30.160
Circumstances don't matter.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:31.600
Bad is bad.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.010
Whether I remember it or
not doesn't matter either.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:40.260
I probably can't do anything
to change the fact I've hurt you all.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:44.210
But that's exactly why I wanna know.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.710
Just what did I do?

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.000
So I can apologize to you all!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:53.290
A..Apologize, you say?

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:57.800
Enough bullshit!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.460
The only way you can pay for your sins

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:02.680
is to disappear from this world!

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.490
I ain't gonna lose.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.140
To know the truth...

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.020
I'm gonna win for sure!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:32.150
You're saying Kaito really did hurt them?

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:36.320
I, Ana, think there's
more than one truth.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.380
Everything has two sides.

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:44.370
What's visible isn't the only truth.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:08.450
All right, he's caught up.

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.210
I won't lose...

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:14.000
I will not lose!

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:15.810
The Orpheus Ring!

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.250
It's runnin' wild?

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:18.630
I won't forgive him.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:19.980
Freecell...

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:23.110
Kaito Daimon wounded Freecell,

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.890
and I won't forgive him!

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:37.710
Is this really for your friend?

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.780
Is he really your friend?

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.410
Is it really...

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:48.380
Shut up.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.490
Shut up, shut up!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.440
Freecell is my...

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:59.060
my one and only friend!

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:26.300
One more puzzle and Kaito wins!

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.910
But if Kaito wins, that guy will...

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.020
What is it?

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.420
Solve the puzzle!

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:46.680
Solve it!

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.300
Let's stop this!

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:50.820
Victory's decided.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.370
I've won.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.370
There's no reason to keep on going.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:56.480
Just...

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.580
shut your mouth!

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.700
Kaito!

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.970
"Victory's decided," my ass!

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.630
We're just getting started!

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:15.390
Fine! If that's how you want it!

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.790
I'll...

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.430
Why?! Why won't you solve it?

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:34.980
You said this was for Freecell,

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.940
your one friend.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:43.440
Wh..What of it?

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.500
If it were me,

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:49.780
I wouldn't want my friend
to go hurting someone,

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.080
or to get hurt.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.960
It would seem it's concluded.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:01.460
Parting is always painful.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:40.800
Kaito moved the lift and
made it catch on that pole.

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.210
Yoshio, move out!

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:46.520
Here...

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:50.080
You? Why?

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:54.720
The truth is, you wanna be
Freecell's friend, right?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.260
You wanna do puzzles with him, right?

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.010
Then try it.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.310
Start from there, got it?

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:31.020
Lucky for Pinochle, eh?

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:33.530
We were able to destroy the Ring.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.760
No problems there.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:41.000
Let's inform Mr. Herbert that
Mr. Pinochle lost his life.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:43.600
What was that?!

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:49.340
Pinochle is dead?

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:51.530
Yes, it was an accident.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:57.680
I thought he was of little use,

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:00.550
but for him to die before
being of any value...

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.250
He was even worse than a maggot!

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.130
Wh..What are you doing?

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:08.510
Those of the Orpheus Order

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:11.610
were chosen by Mr. Klondike,
knights of valor.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.010
If you are even a shadow of a knight,

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.740
show respect to the dead!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:26.710
You're a fool, Pinochle.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.560
The truth is...

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.620
I hated Mama.

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.170
I'm sorry.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.780
It's all my fault.

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:52.500
Your fault?

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:56.820
Back then, after you broke your promise,

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:02.260
Freecell said he wanted to see you again.

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:04.870
Is that so?

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:08.150
Uh, I never saw him again.

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:11.420
When I heard Freecell's story,

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.390
I said that I would tell you for him,

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:16.280
but...

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.420
You mean you never told him?!

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:19.560
Why not?

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.160
I was scared.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:24.390
I felt like the two of you

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:27.550
would become friends
and I'd be left on my own.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:30.690
I didn't want the truth to be known,

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:32.700
so I lied to Freecell and said

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:35.800
you had spread rumors about him.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:40.930
I said bad things about you
so that he'd believe me.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.290
I talked a lot of talk
and made more friends,

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:47.880
all to spread bad rumors about you.

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:50.060
But that's...

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:53.830
During the puzzle, you said
that Kaito did everything!

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:55.920
You were talkin' about yourself?!

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:58.320
I knew you were lyin'!

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:00.220
No!

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:01.830
I..I'm sorry.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:05.050
But at the time, I'd convinced

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:07.550
myself it was Kaito who had done it.

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:10.350
I don't even know how myself...

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:13.350
A lie, but the truth.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.480
Huh? What's that mean?

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:19.860
He was afraid his lie would be exposed.

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:23.930
That feeling may have
been twisted by the Ring.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.970
I guess you could say his
memory was rewritten.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.480
Huh? His memory rewritten?

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.620
To escape from the fear
of his lies, of his sins,

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:35.150
his memory was rewritten...

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:38.820
To make Kaito do what he'd done.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.700
What's more, with Kaito out of the way,

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:47.400
his lie would be forever unknown,
would become the truth.

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:50.910
Tell me one more thing.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.290
That thing about me making

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.180
Freecell's mom sad and her dying...

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:58.060
Was that true?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.530
I don't know.

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.380
You don't know?

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:05.610
That Kaito broke his promise,

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:08.510
and that Freecell's mother
died are both true.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:13.710
But how those two things are related...

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:15.900
Even I don't know that.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.880
Still, he believes it, doesn't he?

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:22.740
For him, it's the truth.

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:24.620
I really am sorry.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:29.120
Because of me, both Kaito and Freecell...

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.230
I'm the one who broke my promise.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.330
Nothing's gonna change that.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.570
Just get some rest for now.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:40.900
That's right!

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:43.990
Thanks for telling us
all that hard stuff.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.970
You're one of us now, Pinochle!

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.620
I don't know about that.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.330
The jury's still out.

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:54.400
Gammon!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:57.290
Yeah, it's like Gammon said.

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:58.400
Kaito, you too?

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:02.780
I ain't done a puzzle
with the real you yet.

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:08.390
Once you get better, let's
do a puzzle together!

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:10.410
We'll start from there!

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.380
Thank you!

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.150
Freecell...

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.840
I want you to help Freecell too!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:30.450
Save him from the Orpheus Order,

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:31.930
and from Klondike.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.310
Klondike?

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.330
"Civility," my ass!

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:43.170
He's shown no courtesy at all!

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:46.950
A mere child, sullying me
with those dirty hands!

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:50.770
You have failed repeatedly,
and Pinochle is dead.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:56.260
Mr. Klondike is doubting
your ability to lead.

00:21:56.770 --> 00:21:59.270
The idiot died, that's all!

00:21:59.270 --> 00:22:01.800
I had nothing to do with it!

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:03.790
As you say.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:08.470
However, Mr. Klondike is most displeased.

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.280
My subordinates don't apologize,

00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:14.740
my boss misunderstands me...

00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:18.350
What kind of unlucky
star was I born under?

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:23.620
There is but one way to
appease Mr. Klondike's anger.

00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:25.210
What is it?

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:25.990
Tell me already.

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:29.170
It's...

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.230
Kaito Daimon!

00:24:04.230 --> 00:24:07.670
It seems you have finally
made me take this seriously.

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:11.320
God Himself would fall prostrate
before this puzzle I've made!

00:24:11.320 --> 00:24:13.740
It simply cannot be solved!

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:17.010
All of you, come challenge it together!

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:20.950
Next time, "Regarding That Man, Herbert"

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:26.900
Regarding That Man, Herbert

00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:22.620
Well, now I shall show you.

00:24:22.620 --> 00:24:25.250
This thank-you party, let's begin!
